      "cooked": "<p>Hi, folks--</p><p>Probably a dumb question here, but I was wondering about Parse's \"Critical Multiplier\" card. Card says the effect goes off \"whenever you discard a card from hand.\"</p><p>So for single-card discards (like \"Segmentation Fault\") this obviously means you get to pop a +1 bonus on someone, which is nice.</p><p>But what about cards that allow multiple discards (or force them) as a single effect? Examples would be Parse's own \"Recompile\" or the various environment cards that are destroyed by discarding your whole hand. In these cases, do you get:</p><p>A) A single +1 bonus for the entire discard action, or</p><p>B) One +1 bonus for EACH card discarded?</p><p>Under A, I discard a theoretical 10 cards when discarding my hand and grant only +1. Under B, I instead grant +10 overall using the same discard.</p><p>Any help would be appreciated. Thanks!</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:40:38.600Z",
