      "raw": "<p>Hi, folks--</p><p>Probably a dumb question here, but I was wondering about Parse&#39;s &quot;Critical Multiplier&quot; card. Card says the effect goes off &quot;whenever you discard a card from hand.&quot;</p><p>So for single-card discards (like &quot;Segmentation Fault&quot;) this obviously means you get to pop a +1 bonus on someone, which is nice.</p><p>But what about cards that allow multiple discards (or force them) as a single effect? Examples would be Parse&#39;s own &quot;Recompile&quot; or the various environment cards that are destroyed by discarding your whole hand. In these cases, do you get:</p><p>A) A single +1 bonus for the entire discard action, or</p><p>B) One +1 bonus for EACH card discarded?</p><p>Under A, I discard a theoretical 10 cards when discarding my hand and grant only +1. Under B, I instead grant +10 overall using the same discard.</p><p>Any help would be appreciated. Thanks!</p>",
